A `[@@@css.merges]` operand that names a binding generate can not find (a
module outside this run, or a value that is not a `[%css]` binding) is
ignored with no error. The merge still orders the operands it can resolve:
here `M.base`'s `margin: 0` before the inline block's `margin-top: 4px`,
which definition order alone would put first.

  $ cat > m.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("._a_top{margin-top:4px;}", "_a_top", "0,1,0 own", "margin", 8, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_all{margin:0;}", "_a_all", "0,1,0 own", "margin", 15, false)]
  > [@@@css.bindings [("M.base", "_id_base", "_a_all")]]
  > [@@@css.blocks [(1, "", [0]); (2, "_id_base", [1])]]
  > [@@@css.merges [(3, ["Other.missing"; "M.base"; 0; "M.notCss"])]]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_all{margin:0;}
  ._a_top{margin-top:4px;}

A merge where no operand resolves adds nothing:

  $ cat > n.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ("._a_top{margin-top:4px;}", "_a_top", "0,1,0 own", "margin", 8, false)]
  > [@@@css ("._a_all{margin:0;}", "_a_all", "0,1,0 own", "margin", 15, false)]
  > [@@@css.merges [(3, ["Other.a"; "Other.b"])]]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate n.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_top{margin-top:4px;}
  ._a_all{margin:0;}
